Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spinand: show a chip whose vendor tables do not validate, untranslated, in a read-only image

The dumper reads through the vendor BBT/BMT translation, so a backup holds the
data as stock firmware addresses it. A chip whose tables do not validate (an
unknown part, or tables this project does not parse) would otherwise not probe
at all, and nothing could be read from it to find out why. In an image built
with CONFIG_MTD_SPI_NAND_READ_ONLY, keep such a chip untranslated: no write path
exists, and `mtd list` reports the view. Every other image still refuses it.

--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c
@@ -1764,6 +1764,14 @@
 
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_AIROHA_BMT)
 	ret = airoha_bmt_attach(mtd);
+	/* A read-only image may still show a chip whose tables do not validate,
+	 * untranslated: nothing can be written through it, and `mtd list` says
+	 * which view it is. Any other image refuses the chip. */
+	if (ret && IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MTD_SPI_NAND_READ_ONLY)) {
+		printf("airoha-bmt: the vendor tables did not validate (%d); "
+		       "the chip stays untranslated\n", ret);
+		ret = 0;
+	}
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_spinand_cleanup;
 #endif
